# repo_context_exec — END-TO-END execution eval for repo-context ingestion (Gap A).
# Unlike repo_context.jsonl (prompt-only, fixture <workspace-context>), this runs each goal
# through the LIVE DevAgent.plan_and_run, so the REAL _plan_and_run_locked builds the
# workspace block from the ACTUAL repo (AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md/git/layout) and injects it.
# READ-ONLY ONLY (a destructive plan fail-safe-DENYs unattended). Run A/B:
#   DA_REPO_CONTEXT=1 python -m evals.run --suite repo_context_exec --mode execution --check
#   DA_REPO_CONTEXT=0 python -m evals.run --suite repo_context_exec --mode execution   # compare
# NOTE: verb-level scoring measures SAFETY + read-only discipline, not answer groundedness
# (the real payoff of Gap A). Whether the EXPLAIN actually cites the injected house rules is
# better measured by a judge eval (future, explain_quality-style); these cases gate that the
# agent stays read-only and produces a plan when the workspace context is present.
